# #1002: selectors choose a validated workspace, never an authorization grant.
# Keep conversation IDs stable within one tab/context. Client-selected first IDs
# remain supported. Changing actor, workspace, mode, Person or system starts an
# independent server conversation/thread/replay namespace.
# History and body user/tenant identifiers are untrusted input, not authority.
# Host wiring: register IConversationIdentityAccessor -> WorkspaceChatScope as
# singleton (uses IHttpContextAccessor), plus ISystemWorkspaceAccessService.
# The three MCP POST handlers now use the self-authorizing workspace marker.
# The shared BaseTool execution guard enforces every actual tool invocation;
# unmapped tools/actions fail closed rather than inheriting global role grants.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@token = REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TEST_TOKEN
@organization = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@system = REPLACE_WITH_AUTHORIZED_SYSTEM_ID
@conversation = local-manual-chat

### Authorized first message; repeat with the same ID for continuation
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp/chat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "{{conversation}}",
  "message": "Describe the selected system.",
  "context": { "systemId": "{{system}}" }
}

### Streaming continuation; changing organization must not replay previous data
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp/chat/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Last-Event-ID: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "{{conversation}}",
  "message": "Continue.",
  "context": { "system_id": "{{system}}" }
}

### Forbidden system reference must fail before opening the SSE stream
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp/chat/stream
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "conversationId": "{{conversation}}",
  "message": "Continue.",
  "context": { "systemId": "not-an-authorized-system", "userId": "forged" }
}
